otten from  friends who have read the book is it's  funny  it's human  it's moving  it's  i had lunch with someone yesterday who  knew firsthand about all the experience  he said at times he was it's hilarious  he was sitting there his wife would say  would call out what are you laughing  about he'd sit there in his chair and  just laugh and laugh  speaking of  what i assume you consider to be a  hilarious moment tell us the story  please about  the gorbachev reagan meeting in the  pantry  this was a strange episode  excuse me  we had  they had had a joint press conference in  geneva  it had two days together for the first  summit  and we were upstairs to say goodbye to  each other and everything like that  now the people were  waiters were passing out champagne there  was a little chit chat it was supposed  to be a 15 minute  goodbye  all of a sudden gorbachev says as we're  standing in a little circle gorbachev  says to reagan let me talk to you for  one minute alone  oregon says okay  the two of them go off into the pantry  upstairs in this international hall  leaving i'm sure the waiters and the  cooks amazed that the two most important  people in the world are suddenly in  their domain of the kitchen  and we're there  schultz myself and the whole u.s  allegation 10 of us or so  within a minute the two  [Music]  reagan and gorbachev come back  gorbachev says to reagan that was our  seventh time together  reagan says oh no this is our first  summit  brain says oh no this is our seventh  time together  reagan has a strange look on his face  and says  oh this was the 11th u.s soviet summit  since 1946 or something  and gorbachev  it's our seventh time  and reagan turns to all of us standing  there and says what do you think he  means  and i never  shy myself i said i don't know mr  president but maybe he means that this  was the seventh time the two of you  had time alone  reagan has a pain look on his face  he says is that what you mean  and gorbachev lights up he says yeah  that's exactly what i mean it's our  seventh time alone  reagan says  thinking of you know they were alone for  30 seconds didn't do anything  reagan says well it doesn't matter how  many times it is it matters what you get  done  and with that they toast and it's  goodbye  it took me a few months to figure out  what the hell was going on there  and then i pieced it together  here was gorbachev being a classic  western style politician  you could have a governor  or a senator or a congressman  go  and tell his people that seven meetings  with the president united states  which is much better than six or five  so we would consider abnormal behavior  for most mortals  normal for our politicians  is extremely abnormal for the  general secretary of the communist party  of the soviet union but that is exactly  what gorbachev wanted to do he wanted to  click up the number of meetings alone  with the president united states so he  could tell his friends and tell his  buddies and tell people back home  it's a revealing moment  because gorbachev is such an unusual  soviet leader  there's another moment that's way off  this subject  when  in reykjavik  ronald reagan's son  was present  looking different and acting different  than the rest that's in geneva  and by the way you write about three  summits in here that you were in  attendance and you write about the  moscow summit and what's the fifth  fifth was that u.n meeting that meeting  in december  what was that little incident well it  was strange  this was the first summit first u.s  soviet summit in seven and a half years  first time gorbachev and reagan had ever  either of them been in the summit first  time they would have met  spent the morning together we were  supposed to have lunch  with the president at 12 noon after the  first morning  we were at the chateau in geneva waiting  and they're  walking in about 11 30 or 4 to 12 is  ron  reagan jr  with some kind of balloon pants and some  kind of  real chic shirt  and looking real mod and cool  and  he had been and worn a credential  as a  journalist from playboy magazine  so reagan comes out of the about 12 15  he's about 15 minutes late president  comes out of his  motorcade in his limousine  and walks in the house  first person he mates is the son  the correspondent for playboy magazine  if anybody would have told me that the  first person  meet the president united states after  his first meeting with gorbachev  and the soviet leader is a correspondent  for playboy magazine i would have  doubted  anyway there he was and ron junior says  dad where were you you're late  and reagan looks at him you know it's  not an usual thing normal thing to tell  president you know you kept us waiting  you just wait for a present so reagan  says to well you know what happened we  have these translations  and it takes so much time he'll say  something  i'll say something in english will be  translated translated translated he said  it's just like the movies where you see  people talk talk talk talk talk in the  foreign films and on the bottom of the  screen flash that's fine  guest is ken edelman this is the book  the great universal embrace talking  about  symmetry and the subtitle there armed  summitry a skeptic's account  when you see a headline in the paper  that says you asked to go to a summit  with the soviet union what do you think  today  i think that a summit is  like cleopatra  it's awfully fun to be involved with but  it's quite treacherous  why  a lot can happen wrong in summits  we've seen that obviously in the munich  summit in 1938 we saw that in the vienna  summit of 1961  where john f kennedy  and  nikita khrushchev just didn't get along  which is fine but khrushchev walked out  thinking that kennedy was a wimp and  even worse yet  kennedy walked out thinking khrushchev  thought he was a wimp  and within a few months of that very  hasty summit ill-prepared summit  silly summit really  within a very few months of 