r the summit  god knows i didn't know what i was  getting into with that but anyway i was  there i got the  remarks done  for the president next day shipped them  in the morning they were there for  reagan to see when they got up and for  bud mcfarland for george schultz to see  when they got up  everybody just thought they were fine  and there  two hours later with miquel gorbachev  and ronald reagan on the stage at the  international meeting place in geneva  president gets up and i just hear him  read my own words that are now six hours  old  usually the way government works you  would have such a process of grinding  and bumping and and such a group grope  on that kind of endeavor of presidential  remarks but here in summits for better  for worse you have a clear shot at the  man you list the four key questions that  you put in this speech but then the  sentence below that jumps out certainly  the president never expressed  the least interest in these questions  either then or subsequently so he got up  and read a speech included your four  questions in it didn't care about him we  sitting out here watching it  should have taken it all seriously or  should well that's one of the mysteries  of ronald reagan he could at times be so  seized with an issue  like sdi handle it beautifully  really do the right thing at other times  um  various issues like  criteria on soviet behavior you couldn't  care less  i guess i want to ask you whether all  that language around summits and  speeches and things like that based on  this story mean anything  most of it doesn't  one of the mysteries of this business  that we spend enormous time grafting  these communiques  for summits  days  previous administration spent months  doing it  they have a half-life of a few hours i  would say press we spend enormous time  drafting them  press grabs thousands of copies  hurriedly to file  for them  and then  [Music]  a few days later no one remembered the  first thing about them including t